            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0114" n="29" xml:id="pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1566: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-08T11:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1919,
                                11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.32
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following enactment by Congress of all election reform measures indorsed by him,
                    General Crowder sailed last midnight for New York on board cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cuba</hi> which is making trip for another purpose. The
                    Cuban Congress voted thanks to Crowder and University of Habana bestowed
                    degree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
